    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4285" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atrĕbătes</span></b> , um,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτρέβατοι</span>
		Strab., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτρεβάτιοι</span> Ptolem., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people in</i> Gallia
			Belgica, now <i>Artois</i> or <i>Dép. du Pas de Calais</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 2,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 23</span></i>; 7, 75; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 17,
				31, § 106</span></i>.—In sing.:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atrĕ-bas</span></b> ,
				ătis, m., <i>an Atrebatian</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 4, 35</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Atrĕbătĭcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Atrebatian</i>:
			sagum, Treb. Gall. 6.</div>
